G1658.definition:
ἐλεύθερος , -α, -ον 
 [in LXX chiefly for חׇפְשִׁי ;] 
 free ; 
 __(a)  in civil sense, not a slave :  Jhn.8:33 ,  1Co.7:21-22 12:13 ,  Gal.3:28 ,  Eph.6:8 ,  Col.3:11 ,  Rev.6:15 13:16 19:18 ; fem.,  Gal.4:22-23, 30 ; 
 __(b)  as regards restraint and obligation in general :  Mat.17:26 ,  1Co.9:1 ; before ἐκ,  1Co.9:19;  ἀπό,  Rom.7:3;  with inf.,  1Co.7:39;  from the law,  Gal.4:26 ,  1Pe.2:16 ;  from sin,  Jhn.8:32, 36 ; τῇ δικαιοσύνῃ, as regards righteousness,  Rom.6:20  (Cremer, 249).†
 (AS)
